= The Directory

The beaten rising, the putsch in Munich and the ruined currency have done what the Kapp putsch could not. In December the Reichstag is adjourned without a date. General von Seeckt announces a Directory of national men: himself, the industrialist Otto Wiedfeldt, Kahr from Bavaria, a banker, a judge. The President signs, because the army has told him he will.

The Directory dissolves the state governments of Saxony and Thuringia for good, places the unions under supervision, and makes membership of the Communist Party a crime punishable by prison. The SPD protests and is banned in Saxony a week later. The Republic of Weimar ends without a shot.

- @underground: Go underground and prepare for a long night.
- @exile: Send the leadership abroad, and keep the party alive from Prague and Moscow.

@underground
subtitle: The party survives as a conspiracy.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 3;
!}

The Zentrale disappears into safe flats and allotment huts. It will be years before it holds a meeting in daylight again.

- @end: See how it ends.

@exile
subtitle: The leaders live; the party at home is on its own.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ending_id = 3;
Q.independence -= 10;
!}

The leaders cross into Czechoslovakia by night through the forests of the Erzgebirge. In Germany, the cells carry on without them.

- @end: See how it ends.

@end
